The given input is already in the correct structured JSON format. If you want to add more properties to each item in the `output_list`, you could follow this format:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "batchTransfer",
            "vulnerability": "Multiple Transfers in One Call",
            "criticism": "This function allows multiple transfers to be made in a single call, which can be used for malicious purposes.",
            "correctness": 7,
            "severity": 5,
            "profitability": 8,
            "additional_property_1": "<value>",
            "additional_property_2": "<value>",
            ...
        }
    ]
}
```

Replace `<value>` with the actual values of your choice.

For example, if you want to add `"bug_type"` and `"detection_tool"` properties, your input might look like this:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "batchTransfer",
            "vulnerability": "Multiple Transfers in One Call",
            "criticism": "This function allows multiple transfers to be made in a single call, which can be used for malicious purposes.",
            "correctness": 7,
            "severity": 5,
            "profitability": 8,
            "bug_type": "Transaction",
            "detection_tool": "Smart Contract Analysis"
        }
    ]
}
```